{%- comment -%}
  Purelane product image.

  The prototype hardcoded 14 base64 SVG bottles into CSS custom properties and
  painted them as background-image. Three problems that mattered in production:
    1. background-image is invisible to the preload scanner, so the hero visual
       could never be the discovered-early LCP element.
    2. Nothing was merchant-editable — a new product meant a new CSS variable.
    3. No intrinsic size, so every card shifted as art loaded (CLS).

  This renders the real Shopify image as an <img> with srcset and explicit
  width/height. When a product has no image — a required seed case — it falls
  back to a branded bottle silhouette that keeps the same aspect ratio, so the
  grid never collapses.

  Params:
    product   - product object (required unless image given)
    art       - 'label' for the labelled bottle (shop cards), otherwise the
                flat silhouette used everywhere else
    image     - explicit image object (optional, wins over product)
    sizes     - sizes attribute (default '(min-width: 860px) 260px, 45vw')
    priority  - true to eager-load + fetchpriority=high (hero only)
    class     - extra classes applied to the img / placeholder
    alt       - alt override; defaults to product title
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  # The prototype draws its products two ways, and which one it uses depends on
  # where the product is standing.
  #
  #   flat   the pale silhouette from the --p-* custom properties. Used by the
  #          hero stage, the rotator, the combo trays, the bundle tiers, the
  #          range strip and the category tiles — every place a product is one
  #          element of a group, where a legible label would be noise.
  #   label  the fully drawn bottle: trigger head, glass highlights, floor
  #          shadow, and a label with the leaf mark, the PURELANE wordmark,
  #          the product name and the fill volume. Used on the shop cards,
  #          where the product is the subject.
  #
  # A Shopify product has one featured image, so each carries both: media 1 is
  # the silhouette and media 2 the labelled bottle. Passing art: 'label' takes
  # the second, and falls back to the featured image when a product only has
  # one — a merchant uploading a single photo still gets a working card.
  assign art_image = product.featured_image
  if art == 'label' and product.images.size > 1
    assign art_image = product.images[1]
  endif

  assign img = image | default: art_image
  assign alt_text = alt | default: img.alt | default: product.title
  assign img_sizes = sizes | default: '(min-width: 860px) 260px, 45vw'

  assign loading_attr = 'lazy'
  assign priority_attr = 'auto'
  if priority
    assign loading_attr = 'eager'
    assign priority_attr = 'high'
  endif

  assign img_class = 'pl-pimg'
  if class != blank
    assign img_class = img_class | append: ' ' | append: class
  endif
-%}

{%- comment -%}
  Truthiness rather than `!= blank` for the object test. Both are correct on
  Shopify, but only nil-falsiness is unambiguous across Liquid implementations,
  and this snippet's whole job is the branch where the image is absent.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if img -%}
  {{
    img
    | image_url: width: 800
    | image_tag:
      loading: loading_attr,
      fetchpriority: priority_attr,
      decoding: 'async',
      widths: '120, 180, 240, 320, 420, 560, 800',
      sizes: img_sizes,
      alt: alt_text,
      class: img_class
  }}
{%- else -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    No-image fallback. Keeps the 0.639 bottle aspect ratio the real shots use, so
    a product without art occupies exactly the same box as one with art.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- assign uid = product.id | default: section.id | default: 'x' -%}
  <span
    class="{{ img_class }} pl-pimg--empty"
    role="img"
    aria-label="{{ alt_text | escape }} — product photo coming soon"
  >
    <svg viewBox="0 0 380 595" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
      <defs>
        <linearGradient id="pl-empty-{{ uid }}" x1="0" y1="0" x2="1" y2="1">
          <stop offset="0" stop-color="#6b55b8" stop-opacity=".38"/>
          <stop offset="1" stop-color="#6b55b8" stop-opacity=".18"/>
        </linearGradient>
      </defs>
      <rect x="149.9" y="0" width="80.1" height="59.5" rx="17.6" fill="#6b55b8" opacity=".3"/>
      <rect x="161.2" y="53.6" width="57.7" height="41.7" fill="#6b55b8" opacity=".24"/>
      <rect x="72.2" y="119" width="235.6" height="476" rx="37.7" fill="url(#pl-empty-{{ uid }})"/>
      <rect x="100.5" y="261.8" width="179.1" height="161.8" rx="11.8" fill="#faf7fd" opacity=".7"/>
      <path d="M190 316c0 22-12 37-27 42 0-22 12-37 27-42Zm0 0c0 22 12 37 27 42 0-22-12-37-27-42Z" fill="#6b55b8" opacity=".34"/>
    </svg>
  </span>
{%- endif -%}
